    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>the points of a predicate with the degrees of their perturbation, which moves them in stages: at stage s = 1, ..., <ref refid="classMR_1_1detail_1_1PerturbationStages_1a703fc73b301b3862535a5f24f658acda" kindref="member">numStages()</ref> only the points with the s smallest ids are perturbed (orient3dPoly leaves the others unperturbed); a polynomial of the predicate that is not zero at stage s already has the leading term of the full one, since every term with a point of a later stage has a larger degree than every term without; and if it was zero at stage s - 1, its terms without the points of stage s cancel one another, so only the products of the terms of degrees from place( s ) up remain (see <computeroutput>from</computeroutput> in lowestTermOfSumOfProducts) </para>
    </detaileddescription>
